            <ArticleTitle>Denial: an adaptive response.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>102-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Denial is a common nursing diagnosis for cardiac patients; yet, not all denial situations are bad. This author describes when denial is actually a successful coping mechanism and describes how to decide when to intervene and when to allow the patient to use this coping technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
